    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d682-a3">

                <pb facs="1181" n="1087" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg1087"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inciosnre 3 in No. 276.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Munif Pacha</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 12,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inclose, in
                    accordnace with your request, a list of the schools closed in Syria.</p>
                <p>It is admitted by your local authorities that many of these schools were doing a
                    useful work by improving the welfare and intelligence of the people.</p>
                <pb facs="1182" n="1088" xml:id="pg1088"/>
                <p>I should be greatly obliged to you if you would give directions to the provincial
                    governor to allow these schools to be reopened immediately, provided that they
                    apply for permission in accordance with the existing law.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton King</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
